{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"title":"Declaring Systems","anchor":"Declaring-Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"title":"System Parameters","anchor":"System-Parameters"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Declaring Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a type with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method that a schedule calls once per run. The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro turns a structure into a system from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Each parameter’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type says what part of the world the system works on and whether it reads or writes it, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":" is always exact, and a schedule can run systems that don’t conflict at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same time."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Read and Write Components","anchor":"Read-and-Write-Components"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Take a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to read components, and iterate it as you would a world’s query","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"results. Take an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to change them in place. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"update can also read other components with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Over","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and narrow the entities it visits with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Where","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Climb {","    func run(_ climbers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        climbers { position, row in","            position.y += abs(row.components.dy)","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let climber = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: -3))","let statue = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: -3), Frozen())","Schedule { Climb() }.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: climber].y)","\/\/ Prints \"3.0\"","print(world[Position.self, of: statue].y)","\/\/ Prints \"0.0\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Climb"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Frozen"},{"type":"text","text":". It conflicts with any system that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Frozen"},{"type":"text","text":", or reads or writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":", and runs at the same time as any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Read and Write Resources and Events","anchor":"Read-and-Write-Resources-and-Events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a resource and a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" changes one. An "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends events, and an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the events sent since the system last read them. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"following schedule sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Damage"},{"type":"text","text":" event for each entity below the ground, then applies the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"damage to its target’s health:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: -1), Health(current: 30))","","let frame = Schedule {","    UpdateEvents()","    Combat()","    ApplyDamage().after(Combat.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Health.self, of: knight].current)","\/\/ Prints \"20\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Combat"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" declares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplyDamage"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Spawn and Despawn Entities","anchor":"Spawn-and-Despawn-Entities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A system that runs alongside others can’t spawn or despawn entities directly, because that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes every component type at once. Take an ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" instead, and queue","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the changes. Commands apply at the end of the wave the system runs in, so systems ordered after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it see them:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct RemoveDefeated {","    func run(_ fighters: Query<Health>, _ commands: inout Commands) {","        for (entity, health) in fighters where health.current <= 0 {","            commands.despawn(entity)","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 12))","Schedule { RemoveDefeated() }.run(on: &world)","","print(world.contains(knight))","\/\/ Prints \"false\"","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A commands parameter conflicts with nothing, so it doesn’t stop a system from running at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time as others.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Take the Whole World","anchor":"Take-the-Whole-World"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method that takes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout World"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a system that can change anything. Its access is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", so a schedule runs it alone, after the systems written before it and before those written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after it. Use one for work that touches many types at once, such as loading a level."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To write a system by hand instead of with the macro, conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", implement","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and declare an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" listing every type the system reads and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Run on the Main Actor","anchor":"Run-on-the-Main-Actor"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mark a system type, or its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"text":" method, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":" to make a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"},{"text":", which a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs on the main actor after the other systems of its wave. Use one to carry results","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the world to a user interface.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Commands":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","title":"Commands","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recorded."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"title":"run(in:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world.","type":"text"}],"required":true},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","title":"access","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"required":true,"defaultImplementations":1,"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","title":"EventWriter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EventReader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"type":"topic","title":"Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"title":"ResourceReader","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceReader","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceReader","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads a resource."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","type":"topic","title":"ResourceWriter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","title":"RemovedComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"System"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","title":"System()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"type":"topic","title":"MainActorSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"title":"Query","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}]}}}